id: pm-vcs-release-caller-rollout
title: Adopt the released reusable Daily Release caller
description: "Fleet rollout for unbraind/pm-ops#272 after the successful pm-jira cross-repository OIDC pilot. Replace copied release orchestration with the released SHA caller, matching validator, explicit empty changelog hooks and package-owned caller contracts. No merge, dispatch or publication."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: "area:release","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#272","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#207"
created_at: "2026-11-14T22:26:50.942Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-19T02:16:57.475Z"
author: codex-ops272-1114
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T22:27:00.144Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Orient and start the authorized fleet rollout. Verified released v2026.11.14 at 7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c. Preserve this package approval, schedule, preparation and publication hooks through canonical inputs. The merged Jira pilot proves cross-repository npm identity acceptance; this package must still pass its own first-run preflight. Run caller contracts, installed attestation, strict YAML, actionlint and regenerated changelog checks. Shared-runner hold gates every push. No review-thread action, merge, dispatch or publication."
  "2026-11-14T22:40:31.059Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Rolled the Jira pilot contract into this package: released workflow pin 7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c (v2026.11.14), exact pm-ops 2026.11.14 validator, explicit include-empty changelog generation/check/notes hooks, and declared yaml for caller tests. Preserved package-owned approval, schedule and preparation inputs. Focused gates passed 70/70, zero failures/skips; linked caller test passed 6/6 in a scratch pm project to avoid tracker run artifacts. Reverting only release.yml to the old copy in a disposable fixture failed 5 of 6 contracts. Actionlint passed 1/1, strict workflow/Dependabot YAML parsing 2/2, installed publish-attestation passed 1/1. Regenerate changelog and check after this final tracker write. Full npm/Bun certification remains with CI; no full local pass is claimed. Cross-repository npm OIDC evidence is Jira run 43639146392, recorded on pm-ops#272; first package activation must still pass its preflight. This package has no npm trusted publisher: releases remain red at the OIDC step until the owner configures the publisher for this repository and release.yml. Every push waits on the shared-runner hold. No merge, dispatch, publication or review-thread action. Leave this item open and release only this author claim."
  "2026-11-15T02:49:11.044Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Round 2 CI follow-up: canonical tag lookup can return unverified-offline. The old inline-publisher success-message assertion then fails despite a valid caller. Update the package attestation test to assert structured recognition, require an explicit deferral without an attestation claim offline, and preserve all refusal checks. Prove it with forced offline execution in a disposable Git fixture; keep coverage source inventory and thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T03:10:29.365Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Round 2 attestation follow-up: targeted tests passed 14/14, including the retained caller and package behavior contracts. Forced offline verification explicitly reports unverified-offline and defers attestation; it never claims verified provenance. In a disposable Git fixture, the fixed assertion passes, reverting only to the old assertion fails, and restoring the fix passes. Unattested-publish refusal checks remain intact. Typecheck and lint passed; coverage source inventory and thresholds remain unchanged. Linked tests passed in a copied scratch tracker. Regenerate and check the changelog after this final write. Exact pushed-head npm/Bun coverage and release certification remain CI gates. No merge, release dispatch, publication or review-thread action."
  "2026-11-16T09:08:55.866Z",pi-claude,"Stalled-PR recovery round 3. Root causes of the failing checks: (1) both test jobs failed test-environment's entrypoint audit because the new release-workflow contract test did not isolate before importing the SDK; fixed by importing the session isolation helper as its first statement, matching every other test entrypoint. (2) Node 22 additionally reported a one-descriptor leak in the object-lifetime soak; that test is untouched by this PR and passes locally on repeated runs, so it is treated as a pre-existing runner flake and left for CI to re-verify on the new head. (3) Greptile thread (stale self-host archive) and CodeRabbit thread (release commit carries the preparation stamp outside the bundle source) both addressed: excluded the release candidate stamp from the self-host source set and regenerated the committed bundle so tip-tree equality holds. Coverage retained: unattested-publish refusal checks and caller contracts unchanged; targeted suites 55/55 and the entrypoint audit 6/6 passed locally, plus typecheck and lint."
  "2026-11-16T10:39:21.959Z",codex-sol,"Resuming the existing PR after provider handoff. Local and remote heads agree at 9f81ac2; main is already merged. The new self-host exclusion is valid, but the exact configuration assertion still expects three entries. Update that assertion and retain a regression proving the preparation stamp is excluded. Re-run package gates and regenerate the staged self-host archive after final tracker evidence."
  "2026-11-16T11:07:50.644Z",codex-sol,"Verified both current CI job logs on 9f81ac2: Node 22 and Node 26 fail loadConfig accepts the repository configuration because the expected exclusion list omits the preparation stamp. The Greptile finding is valid. Updated the exact list and added controls that the stamp is excluded while release.yml remains included. Focused release, attestation and self-host suite passes 77/77; linked configuration regression passes 1/1; typecheck, lint, changelog generation and check pass. The earlier archive and stamp-exclusion findings are retained from 9f81ac2. Full npm test remains active under severe shared-host load, with no full pass claimed. The full release check cannot be certified within the requested twenty-minute allowance while its prerequisite suite exceeds that duration. Refresh the staged archive after final tracker writes and verify the committed snapshot before push. No review-thread actions, merge, dispatch or publication."
  "2026-11-16T19:06:15.696Z",codex-sol,"Review round O: pulled fast-forward only and verified supplied PR head. Checking each requested thread against source before changes; will run targeted gates and commit tracker evidence with fixes. No workflow dispatches or review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-16T19:08:39.626Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64C-4Z verified against rollout evidence: trusted publisher is not yet configured. Documentation now instructs the owner to configure this repository and release.yml and states the OIDC release blocker, retaining first-run identity verification. Will stage tracker/doc changes, regenerate selfhost.bundle, commit, then verify committed HEAD before push."
  "2026-11-16T19:10:26.847Z",codex-sol,"Validation passed: npm run typecheck; npm run build:test; npm run lint; linked targeted release-workflow, release-approval, release-preparation and publish-attestation tests; npm run changelog:check; git diff --check. PM test was run in tracker/source mode after correcting an invalid context selection that ran no tests. Next: regenerate staged text self-host archive, commit and verify HEAD; owner npm trusted-publisher setup remains outstanding."
  "2026-11-17T02:17:04.661Z",pi-glm,"Review round AC: merged current main into this PR branch (resolving the selfhost.bundle conflict by regenerating it through the self-host gate), ran npm run build, npm run self-host:write, committed the regenerated bundle, and npm run accept:self-host passes at HEAD: the committed bundle's tip tree is byte-identical to the committed source except validated external action revisions. changelog:check and pm validate pass."
  "2026-11-17T07:58:43.723Z",pi-glm,"Review round AK (thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64SPBm): confirmed from the failed CI run that both required Linux jobs fail only the exact-gates self-host identity test - the committed bundle's tip tree diverged from the committed source on this rollout tracker's task/history files, because the tracker receipt was committed after the bundle. Fix: merged the latest main (dependency-bump conflicts resolved by keeping this branch's newer pm-ops 2026.11.14 pin; no history lines rewritten, the merge auto-merged append-only history cleanly), then ran the self-host gate - commit, build, self-host:write, bundle commit, and accept:self-host at HEAD confirms the committed bundle's tip tree is byte-identical to the committed source. The other logged error (missing-pm-vcs-cli MODULE_NOT_FOUND in the stat-cache acceptance) is the intentional missing-CLI refusal; all remaining 1938 tests passed. Gates: typecheck, lint, changelog:check clean."
  "2026-11-17T17:32:53.491Z",codex-sol,"Round BA: verified review gaps in workflow extraction, run-wide configuration and operand classification, or release-fixture generation order. Implement focused regression controls, retain existing fixture verdicts and run required package gates. No review-thread actions, merge or publication. Leave item open."
  "2026-11-17T17:47:09.800Z",codex-sol,"Verified PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64in0T: the fixture wrote its changelog before executing the release hook, so generation order was untested. Move the write into the changelog:full stub and independently hash the expected generated bytes. The expected bundle hash assertion stays. Release-preparation tests pass 2/2; moving generation after staging fails the mutation control. Typecheck, lint and duplication gates passed. Supplementary bundle-reference tests passed 70/71; the unchanged operational entry-point test hit its existing 60-second child-process timeout while importing the committed archive. A focused retry on the guard branch also timed out at that limit before any BA code commit. No unrelated timeout policy was changed. All tracker evidence is finalized now, including claim release. Next fetch tags, regenerate/check CHANGELOG.md, commit code and tracker, build, regenerate and commit selfhost.bundle, then run accept:self-host at final HEAD with no subsequent tracker writes. Leave items in progress. No review-thread actions, merge, dispatch or publication."
  "2026-11-18T07:16:18.989Z",codex-sol,"Round BX: CI test (22) and test (26) were green on the PR head. The merge with #213 conflicts in the release workflow, release approval test, manifests, and generated self-host bundle. The v2026.11.14 caller and the latest pm-ops release v2026.11.17 both install npm globally in six jobs. pm-ops #289 restores job-local bootstrap and exact version checks but its SHA has no release tag. The workflow and caller validator require an exact matching tag. Kept the PR head parked pending a canonical release with #289, so the release keeps the reusable caller and npm isolation together."
  "2026-11-18T23:59:37.288Z",codex-sol,"Round CY will merge current main, adopt the published pm-ops v2026.11.18 reusable workflow, and verify the release, CI, changelog, and self-host gates."
  "2026-11-19T00:02:19.513Z",codex-sol,"Merged origin/main in 6898d5b and preserved the Round BX receipt. Kept Fleet CI v2, the job-local npm guard and executable-line fixtures, the main pm-changelog version and release metadata, and the reusable caller approval, recovery and package hooks. Seven changed tracker histories retain both parents in timestamp order. Pinned unbraind/pm-ops/.github/workflows/daily-release.yml at c46a2419c63af3b348e6b559b0733ab0d9942cc7 (v2026.11.18)."
  "2026-11-19T00:03:31.476Z",codex-sol,"Local gates passed: global npm guard (288), release approval (35), release preparation (2), CI shards and CodeQL (10), typecheck, build, build:test, lint and changelog:check. The exact pinned workflow passed the unchanged global npm guard and input and permission compatibility checks. Its six npm bootstraps use executable job-local installs and version checks. PM validation found zero history drift and reported existing advisory warnings. The changelog was regenerated after fetching tags. Final self-host acceptance is required at the snapshot commit before push."
  "2026-11-19T01:54:49.551Z",codex-sol,Round DA at PR head 0c9eeb1. The pinned workflow runs its build before changelog generation. Use npm lifecycle ordering to run the archive hook after successful generation and keep release-files staging. The caller already declares and forwards the retirement input. Verify its contract against the reference caller and document the operator procedure.
  "2026-11-19T01:58:26.970Z",codex-sol,"Round DA direct gates passed: 354 focused release, approval, guard and workflow tests with zero failures or skips, typecheck, build:test, lint, and changelog:check. The updated preparation fixture fails on the old script because the generator receives no flags, and verifies the staged changelog in the simulated release commit with the new hook. The pm-rl retirement contract already matches the caller. Follow-up pm-vcs-release-attempt-recovery records the pinned workflow refusal after a publish-attempt record."
  "2026-11-19T02:01:11.588Z",codex-sol,"Round DA thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOToJT7M65RYFP -> ac751f7 (forward include-empty to the changelog generator and regenerate the release bundle in npm postrelease:changelog). PRRT_kwDOToJT7M65RYFK -> 994f379 (existing boolean recovery input and pass-through, matching pm-rl) and ac751f7 (README recovery steps and dedicated workflow contract). The pin refuses retirement after a recorded attempt. Track that upstream limitation in pm-vcs-release-attempt-recovery. accept:self-host passed at ac751f7. A disposable version bump generated and checked the actual changelog and committed the regenerated bundle."
  "2026-11-19T02:14:35.602Z",codex-sol,"Exact-head CI at f34402e found one Round DA fixture defect in the Node 22 quick shard: the synthetic archive script launches git without an explicit child environment. Apply the existing test environment boundary in the fixture and include its entrypoint audit in the focused gates."
  "2026-11-19T02:16:55.459Z",codex-sol,"Round DA follow-up for PRRT_kwDOToJT7M65RYFP: both CI shard 5 jobs on f34402e reported the same implicit environment in the synthetic bundle writer. The fixture now uses testEnvironment for its nested git read. Node 22.18.0 passed both the release-commit fixture and the entrypoint audit, covering 151 test entrypoints and 232 explicit child launches. Typecheck, build:test, lint and changelog:check passed."
